:1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14127},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62313475,"created":"2026-10-16T01:39:43.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":3,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13030,"number":2,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 1:39 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":82017,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":7212,"text":"<p>If $\\overline{C} = \\{ 3.1, 4.3, 5.1, 7.7, 9.5 \\}$ and $\\overline{D} = \\{ 1.8, 2.7, 4.3, 7.7 \\},$ then what is $\\overline{ C \\cup D }?$</p>\n","choice1":"$ \\{ 4.3, 7.7 \\}$","choice2":"$ \\{ 1.8, 4.3, 7.7 \\}$","choice3":"$ \\{2.7, 4.3, 7.7 \\}$","choice4":"$ \\{ 3.1, 5.1, 9.5 \\}$","choice5":"$ \\{ 1.8, 2.3, 3.1, 5.1, 9.5 \\}$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>De Morgan&#39;s law for unions states that\n\\[\n\\overline{C \\cup D} \\equiv \\overline{C} \\cap \\overline{D}.\n\\]</p>\n<p>So, we have</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n\\overline{C \\cup D} &= \\overline{C} \\cap \\overline{D} \\\\[3pt]\n&= \\{ 3.1, 4.3, 5.1, 7.7, 9.5 \\} \\cap \\{ 1.8, 2.7, 4.3, 7.7 \\} \\\\[3pt]\n&= \\{ 4.3, 7.7 \\}.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2788,"name":"De Morgan's Laws for Sets"},"example":{"id":7212,"title":"Finding the Complement of a Union"},"group":{"id":15009,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14252530,"answer":{"id":62313475,"cread":"2026-10-16T01:39:43.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":3,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13030},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62313487,"created":"2026-10-16T01:39:59.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11778,"number":3,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 1:39 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:12","question":{"id":81867,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":7212,"text":"<p>If $\\overline{A} = \\{ x, y, z \\}$ and $\\overline{B} = \\{ w, x, y \\},$ then what is $\\overline{ A \\cup B }?$</p>\n","choice1":"$\\{ x,y \\}$","choice2":"$\\{ x,y,z \\}$","choice3":"$\\{ w,x,y,z \\}$","choice4":"$\\{ x \\}$","choice5":"$\\emptyset$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>De Morgan&#39;s law for unions states that\n\\[\n\\overline{A \\cup B} \\equiv \\overline{A} \\cap \\overline{B}.\n\\]</p>\n<p>So, we have</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n\\overline{A \\cup B} &= \\overline{A} \\cap \\overline{B} \\\\[3pt]\n&= \\{ x,y,z \\} \\cap \\{ w,x,y \\} \\\\[3pt]\n&= \\{ x,y \\}.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2788,"name":"De Morgan's Laws for Sets"},"example":{"id":7212,"title":"Finding the Complement of a Union"},"group":{"id":15009,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14252530,"answer":{"id":62313487,"cread":"2026-10-16T01:39:59.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11778},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62313494,"created":"2026-10-16T01:40:15.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":4,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11640,"number":4,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 1:40 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:12","question":{"id":102567,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":7212,"text":"<p>If $\\overline{X} = \\{ 7,10,12,19,23 \\}$ and $\\overline{Y} = \\{ 8,10,12,14 \\},$ then what is $\\overline{ X \\cup Y }?$</p>\n","choice1":" $\\{ 10,12 \\}$","choice2":" $\\{7,10,12,19,23 \\}$","choice3":" $\\emptyset$","choice4":" $\\{ 8,10,12,14 \\}$","choice5":" $\\{7,8,10,12,14,19,23 \\}$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>De Morgan&#39;s law for unions states that\n\\[\n\\overline{X \\cup Y} \\equiv \\overline{X} \\cap \\overline{Y}.\n\\]</p>\n<p>So, we have</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n\\overline{X \\cup Y} &= \\overline{X} \\cap \\overline{Y} \\\\[3pt]